course: dictionary
lesson: 1622
title: Word in context: chessboard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chessboard is a square board for playing chess or draughts. Its squares are coloured light and dark in turn, and there are 64 of them in eight rows of eight. The word is made of two words you already know: chess and board.
explain: Read the sentence «on a chessboard a chameleon would not turn checked». The words around chessboard give the clue: checked means a pattern of squares, like the light and dark squares on a board. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A board with a pattern of squares.
explain: Another sentence lists things you can check: «let the facts settle it — the chessboard, the score, a photo, a visit». Here chessboard is one of the real things you could look at. The list tells you it is a physical thing, not a feeling or an idea.
fact: A chessboard is a square board with 64 squares.
fact: Chess is played on a chessboard, and draughts is played on one too.
fact: Eight rows of eight make 8 × 8 = 64 squares.
fact: The squares are coloured light and dark in turn, so no two squares next to each other are the same colour.
fact: If you count squares of all sizes on a chessboard, including the big ones made of four small squares, there are 204 squares in all.
exercise: The chessboard has eight rows of eight squares. How many squares are there in all? | 56 | 32 | 81 | *64
exercise: What is a chessboard? | A board for a game with no pieces | A kind of mood | *A square board with 64 squares, for playing chess or draughts | A chameleon's favourite colour
exercise: Find and copy one word from «a chameleon would not turn checked» that describes a pattern of squares. | *checked | would | turn | chameleon
test: How many squares are in each row of a chessboard? | Sixteen | *Eight | Sixty-four | Four
test: Chess and draughts are played on a board. What shape is a chessboard? | Round | Triangle | Oval | *Square
exam: A chessboard has eight rows of eight squares. What is 8 × 8? | 56 | 88 | 16 | *64
